<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Mar base metals import prices up-AFTAK.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Mar base metals import prices up-AFTAK.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's non-ferrous metals import prices rose in March due to gains in world markets, the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea (AFTAK) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Import prices of precious metals were as follows:</p>
<p>(price per tonne on CIF)</p>
<p> METAL		     Origin	Mar	 Feb</p>
<p> Copper (99.95 pct)    Chile     2,500     2,486</p>
<p> Copper scrap (berry)  U.S.	2,513     2,403</p>
<p> Aluminium (99.7 pct)  Australia 1,722     1,700</p>
<p> Lead (99.99 pct)	China	 745	 700</p>
<p> Zinc (99.995 pct)     S.America 1,315     1,271</p>
<p> Nickel (99.9 pct)     Canada    8,150     8,087</p>
<p> Tin (99.85 pct)	 Malaysia  5,840     6,033</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
